        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Edits the registers for the current :cpp:class:`IfContentPart` with state info from
&apos;ini&apos; :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

.. note::
   The base implementation forwards straight to \ref edit and **ignores &apos;ini&apos;
   entirely**, exactly as the pure-Python original does -- see
   :cpp:func:`BaseIniGraphEdit::editFromIni`&apos;s own note
</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>part</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The part of the <computeroutput><ref refid="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_if_template" kindref="compound">IfTemplate</ref></computeroutput> being edited, modified in place </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>sectionName</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The name of the <computeroutput>section</computeroutput>_ being edited </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ini</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
The associated ``.ini`` file -- a **non-owning, nullable** pointer, where
``nullptr`` stands in for &quot;no ``.ini`` file is available&quot; :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

**Default**: ``nullptr``
</verbatim> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>modType</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
The type of mod to fix -- also a **non-owning, nullable** pointer, for the same
reason ``ini`` is one: none of this class&apos;s own subclasses read it, and the
`pybind11`_ layer has no C++ :cpp:class:`ModType` to hand over (the `Python`_ API&apos;s
``ModType`` is still a pure-`Python`_ class of its own) :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

**Default**: ``nullptr``
</verbatim> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>modName</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The name of the mod to fix to. <bold>Default</bold>: <computeroutput>""</computeroutput> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>partRanges</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
The ranges that indicate the valid order indices to process for &apos;part&apos; -- a
**non-owning, nullable** pointer, where ``nullptr`` stands in for the pure-Python
original&apos;s ``partRanges = None`` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

**Default**: ``nullptr``
</verbatim></para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The same part that was passed in, after editing </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
