    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
This class inherits from :cpp:class:`BaseIniGraphPartEdit`

Base class for a filter that edits some registers within an :cpp:class:`IfContentPart`
:raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

.. note::
   This is a class **template**, parameterized by exactly the same ``K``/``V``/``KeyHash``/
   ``KeyEqual`` as the :cpp:class:`IfContentPart` it edits. It has to be: the `Python`_
   binding layer edits ``IfContentPart&lt;py::object, py::object, ...&gt;`` (every key/value that
   crosses the `pybind11`_ boundary is a ``py::object``), while a plain C++ caller normally
   wants ``IfContentPart&lt;std::string, std::string&gt;`` -- which is what ``K``/``V`` default to
   here, so ``BaseRegEdit&lt;&gt;`` reads exactly like the non-templated version this replaced
</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>K</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the keys stored in the parts this edits </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>V</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the values stored in the parts this edits </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>KeyHash</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>A hasher for <computeroutput>K</computeroutput>. Defaults to <computeroutput>std::hash&lt;K&gt;</computeroutput> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>KeyEqual</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>An equality comparator for <computeroutput>K</computeroutput>. Defaults to <computeroutput>std::equal_to&lt;K&gt;</computeroutput> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
